# Network secrets for the ACME simulation cloud environment (cloud environment
# menu -> Edit -> Network secrets). The agent proxy attaches or re-signs with
# these after a request leaves the VM, so the values never reach Claude,
# commands, env vars or files. Never commit real values.

# --- AWS (read-only) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Secret type:   AWS SigV4
# Access key ID / Secret access key:
#                a key for the `claude-code-web` IAM user (acme-sim
#                iac/bootstrap): ReadOnlyAccess minus secret values, state
#                files and credential minting. Leave session token empty.
# Hosts:         *.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com
#                sts.amazonaws.com
#                iam.amazonaws.com
#
# The CLI signs with the session's `proxy-injected` placeholder keys and the
# proxy strips that signature and re-signs as this user, so there is no
# assume-role step: the user itself is the read-only principal. Not covered:
# hosts under *.api.aws (the AWS/EKS MCP endpoints) and `aws eks get-token`,
# whose presigned URL the cluster sends to AWS itself, so kubectl needs its
# own credential from the acme-sim cluster layer.

# --- Not needed --------------------------------------------------------------
#   GitHub: the GitHub proxy authenticates git and the GitHub tools with the
#     Claude GitHub App. Leave GH_TOKEN / GITHUB_TOKEN unset.
#   Honeycomb, Slack: use claude.ai connectors (Honeycomb's EU MCP server is
#     https://mcp.eu1.honeycomb.io/mcp, added as a custom connector).
